# P7 (SOFT, card M only, FIRST of the WP7 jobs): the drafter permutation probe (optimisation/ttnn-op/draft_permute). The SERVED K/V assembly (draft_attention_branch.served_key_value), query fold and output
# unfold (quad_draft_tp, pair_row_exact_tp, octo_draft_tp) run on real ttnn ops on one copy of the same host data, draft_permute_tp's launches (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE) on another; every output pair is read back
# and compared as int16 bit patterns (-0 and +0 differ). Shapes: the quad, the pair (two 2,048-row histories and mixed 256 / 1,024), the octo plan; regimes: random, edge (+-0 and denormals of both signs in the cached
# banks, the live block and the queries) and sweep (all 65,536 bf16 bit patterns laid across each tensor). Beside the verdict arm it runs the OTHER reading of the served concat (cached banks raw) as information.
# WHAT IT DECIDES: whether the kernel's value rule matches the served bytes, and WHICH pieces the rule touches. The CPU proves the kernel equals a MODEL of the served composition (a row-axis slice that starts inside a
# tile and a row-axis concat with a piece that is not a whole number of tiles map a zero exponent to +0, nothing else does). The model is read off the device profile (the quad's concat untilizes the cached banks too:
# four 64-core untilizes a tensor and layer); this job reads the bytes. Then it times both arms under a captured trace (per launch, K and V together; the grid is printed: 13x10 or 11x10).
# READ: 'DRAFT_PERMUTE verdict=PASS' (every compare differing=0, no launch fell back) and 'DRAFT_PERMUTE cached banks: canonical (the model holds)'. FAIL prints the first differing rows by plan piece and value; if the
# cached banks line reads 'raw (flip canon_cached)' the served concat does not round-trip the banks: flip the planner's canon_cached default in draft_permute_tp.py (one word), rebuild the image, rerun. NOT-RUN carries the
# error text. The timing lines (served_us against launch_us per site and shape) are information, not a gate; the gate of the lever is the audited attach and the ABAB on early-draft ms.
# Duration (estimate): 30 min (container timeout 1 h; the probe's own watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards, and the harness refuses while anything else can reach the board.
# The harness's container turns the image's C2 boot hook off (QWEN_C2_SERVING=0) and unsets the baked four-card mesh descriptor; the workflow's cardm step waits for other CI's buildx builders instead of refusing the
# window. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is the image B0 builds (a harness mounts this checkout's scripts/ci whole, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/draft_permute/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
